:"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLUnpitched","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The unpitched type represents musical elements that are notated on the staff but lack definite pitch, such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unpitched percussion and speaking voice. If the child elements are not present, the note is placed on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"middle line of the staff. This is generally used with a one-line staff. Notes in percussion clef should always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use an unpitched element rather than a pitch element.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLUnpitched"}],"title":"MXLUnpitched","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"}}}